        DocumentBuilderFactory factory = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
        Document document = factory.newDocumentBuilder().parse(new java.io.FileReader(filePath));

        Element root = document.getDocumentElement();

        // Accessing elements
        System.out.println(root.getName());
        System.out.println(root.getTextContent());

        // Manipulating XML nodes
        // ...
    }
}
```

This example parses an XML file and prints the contents of each element.

**Using XLSX**

XLSX is a Java library for reading and writing Excel files. Here's an example of using XLSX:

```java
import com.h2p.xlsx.XlsxWriter;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        String filePath = "data.xlsx";
        XlsxWriter writer = new XlsxWriter();

        // Adding a row to the sheet
        writer.addRow(new Object[]{1, 2, 3});

        // Writing data to the file
        writer.write("Sheet1", new int[][]{{1, 4}, {5, 6}});
    }
}
```

This example adds a row to an XLSX file and writes data to it.
